  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "important": false,
  "source": "EAMCET 2012 (Engineering)",
  "question": "Two solid spheres A and B, each of radius $R$, are made of materials of densities $\\rho_A$ and $\\rho_B$ respectively. Their moments of inertia about a diameter are $I_A$ and $I_B$ respectively. The value of $\\dfrac{I_A}{I_B}$ is",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\left(\\dfrac{\\rho_A}{\\rho_B}\\right)^2$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\sqrt{\\dfrac{\\rho_A}{\\rho_B}}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{\\rho_A}{\\rho_B}$",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\dfrac{\\rho_B}{\\rho_A}$",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "Same radius, so $I = \\dfrac{2}{5}mR^2 \\propto m \\propto \\rho$:\n$$\\frac{I_A}{I_B} = \\frac{\\rho_A}{\\rho_B}$$",
